ep_id": "step_16", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 182, "direction": "in", "window": [25832, 27631]}, "result_digest": "836b6ceeaa390382", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 0, \"neighbors\": [], \"node\": 182, \"window\": [25832, 27631]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 45241, "tokens_after": 45241, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_30df0d06", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1006, 1860], "window": [18031, 56431], "confidence": 0.62, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Statically 1006 and 1860 are connected (step_03 shows a dense 2-hop neighbourhood via hubs 45, 153, 182), but the hubs are the confounder: 153/182 have 134/65 partners (step_06) and 45 is a super-hub, so ignoring time almost any pair appears linked. Temporally, 1006's out-neighbours are {45,230,925,1680} and 1860's in-neighbours are {153,182,958,1390} (steps 05, 04) \u2014 disjoint, so a cascade needs at least 3 hops. 1006's outgoing activity is concentrated in a tight cluster around 20732-21631 (steps 09, 11, 13), with only isolated later events (one to 1680 in [37232,42031], one in [46832,51631], step_15). 1860's receptions occur at ~26432-27631 (from 182), ~32432-33631 and ~43232-44431 (steps 10, 12, 14). The nearest candidate reception (182\u21921860 in [26432,27631]) is ~4800+ time units after 1006's last relevant out-event, which would require ~8+ perfectly chained \u2264600 hops; crucially, node 182 received no incoming interaction at all in the 1800 units before it contacted 1860 (step_16), so the required hand-off into the final relay does not exist within the 600-unit limit. The later receptions are even further removed (one precedes 1006's next event entirely). The evidence therefore indicates activity volume and hub popularity, not a genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Statically 1006 and 1860 are connected (step_03 shows a dense 2-hop neighbourhood via hubs 45, 153, 182), but the hubs are the confounder: 153/182 have 134/65 partners (step_06) and 45 is a super-hub, so ignoring time almost any pair appears linked. Temporally, 1006's out-neighbours are {45,230,925,1680} and 1860's in-neighbours are {153,182,958,1390} (steps 05, 04) \u2014 disjoint, so a cascade needs at least 3 hops. 1006's outgoing activity is concentrated in a tight cluster around 20732-21631 (steps 09, 11, 13), with only isolated later events (one to 1680 in [37232,42031], one in [46832,51631], step_15). 1860's receptions occur at ~26432-27631 (from 182), ~32432-33631 and ~43232-44431 (steps 10, 12, 14). The nearest candidate reception (182\u21921860 in [26432,27631]) is ~4800+ time units after 1006's last relevant out-event, which would require ~8+ perfectly chained \u2264600 hops; crucially, node 182 received no incoming interaction at all in the 1800 units before it contacted 1860 (step_16), so the required hand-off into the final relay does not exist within the 600-unit limit. The later receptions are even further removed (one precedes 1006's next event entirely). The evidence therefore indicates activity volume and hub popularity, not a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53631, "total_output_tokens": 10556, "total_tokens": 64187, "total_latency_ms": 149772, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}